ISSUE 3
===================

After creating ingress resource, the ALB address wasnt getting displayed 

 kubectl get ingress -n robot-shop
NAME         CLASS    HOSTS   ADDRESS   PORTS   AGE
robot-shop   alb      *                 80      24s


Step 1: Describe the Ingress — Check Events

kubectl describe ingress robot-shop -n robot-shop
Error found:


Warning  FailedBuildModel  ingress  AccessDenied: Not authorized to perform sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity
Meaning: The controller can't assume its IAM role via IRSA.

Verify OIDC Provider Exists

Step 2:  eksctl utils associate-iam-oidc-provider --cluster three-tier --region us-west-2 --approve
Result: Already associated ✅

Step 3: Get Current Cluster's OIDC ID

aws eks describe-cluster --name three-tier --region us-west-2 \
  --query "cluster.identity.oidc.issuer" --output text
Result: https://oidc.eks.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/id/1B2725ECB6084D0BF5377B816699B8C2

Step 4: Check IAM Role Trust Policy

aws iam get-role --role-name AmazonEKSLoadBalancerControllerRole \
  --query "Role.AssumeRolePolicyDocument" --output json
Finding — Mismatch:

Root Cause
The IAM role was created for a previous cluster with a different OIDC provider. When the new cluster was created, it got a new OIDC ID, but the role's trust policy was never updated. STS rejected the AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity call because the token issuer didn't match.

Fix Applied
1. Updated the Trust Policy with Correct OIDC ID

cat > lb-trust-policy.json << 'EOF'
{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Principal": {
                "Federated": "arn:aws:iam::307946644949:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/id/1B2725ECB6084D0BF5377B816699B8C2"
            },
            "Action": "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
            "Condition": {
                "StringEquals": {
                    "oidc.eks.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/id/1B2725ECB6084D0BF5377B816699B8C2:aud": "sts.amazonaws.com",
                    "oidc.eks.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/id/1B2725ECB6084D0BF5377B816699B8C2:sub": "system:serviceaccount:kube-system:aws-load-balancer-controller"
                }
            }
        }
    ]
}
EOF

aws iam update-assume-role-policy \
  --role-name AmazonEKSLoadBalancerControllerRole \
  --policy-document file://lb-trust-policy.json
2. Restarted the Controller

kubectl rollout restart deployment aws-load-balancer-controller -n kube-system
3. Verified

kubectl get ingress -n robot-shop
ADDRESS now shows ALB DNS name ✅

