ALB Not Reachable — Complete Analysis
Problem Statement
ALB was created with a DNS name but accessing it returned ERR_TIMED_OUT — the application was completely unreachable from the internet.

Two Root Causes Identified
#	Issue	Error
1	Target pod in us-west-2d but ALB only had subnets in us-west-2a and us-west-2b	Target health: "Target.NotInUse" - Target is in an Availability Zone that is not enabled for the load balancer
2	Cluster security group had no inbound rule allowing ALB traffic on port 8080	Target healthy but traffic still couldn't reach pods
How We Identified the Issues
Command 1: Check Target Health

TG_ARN=$(aws elbv2 describe-target-groups --region us-west-2 \
  --query "TargetGroups[?contains(TargetGroupName,'robotsho')].TargetGroupArn" --output text)

aws elbv2 describe-target-health --region us-west-2 \
  --target-group-arn $TG_ARN --output json
→ Revealed: "State": "unused", "Reason": "Target.NotInUse" — AZ mismatch

Command 2: Check ALB Subnets

aws elbv2 describe-load-balancers --region us-west-2 \
  --load-balancer-arns <alb-arn> \
  --query "LoadBalancers[].AvailabilityZones" --output json
→ Revealed: ALB only in us-west-2a and us-west-2b

Command 3: Check Cluster SG Rules

aws eks describe-cluster --name three-tier --region us-west-2 \
  --query "cluster.resourcesVpcConfig.clusterSecurityGroupId" --output text

aws ec2 describe-security-group-rules --region us-west-2 \
  --filters "Name=group-id,Values=sg-00e9a43e7d355558c" --output table
→ Revealed: No inbound rule from ALB SG to pods on port 8080

Fixes Applied
Fix 1: Add Missing AZ Subnet to ALB

aws ec2 create-tags --region us-west-2 \
  --resources subnet-04d719cd2553f7866 \
  --tags Key=kubernetes.io/cluster/three-tier,Value=shared \
         Key=kubernetes.io/role/elb,Value=1

aws elbv2 set-subnets --region us-west-2 \
  --load-balancer-arn <alb-arn> \
  --subnets subnet-0ee0b4a6f0fb1dfbd subnet-032fbfdd0d88c4f27 subnet-04d719cd2553f7866
Fix 2: Allow ALB to Reach Pods

aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress --region us-west-2 \
  --group-id sg-00e9a43e7d355558c \
  --protocol tcp \
  --port 8080 \
  --source-group sg-03d0f9216d6531572

